{"title": "TUM VI", "parts": {"header": "<div class=\"sd ex-sd\"><div class=sd-grid><div class=sd-head><span class=\"sd-maker none\">TUM Computer Vision Group</span><h1 id=\"_top\">TUM VI</h1><p class=sd-type>Stereo 1024² fisheye + BMI160 @ 200 Hz</p></div><figure class=sd-plate><div class=sd-frame><img src=\"/media/examples/tum-vi/tum-vi-rig.jpg\" alt=\"TUM VI sensor rig: two fisheye cameras, IMU board and a small PC, with motion-capture markers\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\"></div><figcaption><a href=\"https://cvg.cit.tum.de/data/datasets/visual-inertial-dataset\">Photo: TUM Computer Vision Group, TUM VI dataset page, CC BY 4.0 ↗︎</a></figcaption></figure><div class=sd-cta><div class=sd-buttons><a class=\"sd-btn primary\" href=\"https://cvg.cit.tum.de/data/datasets/visual-inertial-dataset\">Downloads: TUM VI dataset page ↗︎</a><a class=\"sd-btn\" href=\"/benchmark/results/tum-vi/\">All recordings and tools: Dataset eval →</a></div></div><div class=sd-specs><dl class=sd-rows><div class=sd-row><dt>Cameras</dt><dd>2 × 1024² global-shutter fisheye, 20 Hz</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>IMU</dt><dd>Bosch BMI160, 200 Hz</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Board</dt><dd>AprilGrid 6×6, tag 88 mm</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Format</dt><dd>ROS1 bag</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Licence</dt><dd>CC BY 4.0</dd></div></dl></div></div></div>", "glance": "<p>One MVIS camera + IMU run on dataset-calib-imu1, and how close it lands to TUM&#x27;s published Kalibr calibration.</p><div class=band><figure class=demo><video src=\"/media/hero/hero_tumvi_960.mp4\" poster=\"/media/hero/hero_tumvi_960.jpg\" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload=metadata></video><figcaption>The scene MVIS recovered from this dataset, as on the homepage. The values beside it come from this page&#x27;s run.</figcaption></figure><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.10<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0–cam1 baseline</span><b>101.1<small> mm</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>+0.16<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>94.9<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div><p class=sd-note>Reprojection is how far, in pixels, the detected corners lie from where the solve puts them. td is the camera–IMU time offset, and the lever arm is the camera–IMU position offset.</p>", "process": "<p>MVIS's own player, from this run: the detected board corners, then the rig's path as the solve refines it. Press <b>Play</b> or drag the bar; pick a camera card to look through that camera. We publish no camera images.</p><div class=proc-wrap><button type=button class=proc-open hidden><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 220\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"196.0,157.7 288.3,200.0 305.0,62.3 212.7,20.0 196.0,157.7\" fill=\"var(--strong)\" fill-opacity=\".1\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\"/><polyline points=\"174.8,103.2 184.6,98.7 172.2,100.4 146.0,98.1 125.0,95.3 118.8,95.0 125.6,93.5 143.8,93.8 166.7,97.2 182.4,100.8 180.3,103.0 162.5,98.3 138.3,96.0 123.0,98.6 123.0,97.2 133.1,95.6 151.9,96.9 166.0,101.3 170.6,105.1 160.9,102.8 143.1,100.5 126.8,98.0 121.1,96.8 123.9,97.9 127.9,82.5 129.9,57.1 129.7,45.7 132.8,69.4 135.6,104.5 134.7,125.8 134.3,122.9 136.9,91.7 134.7,58.2 131.9,45.1 132.8,63.9 134.3,102.9 132.6,132.8 130.3,144.8 135.2,120.5 138.1,78.9 135.4,45.2 135.2,50.5 136.8,90.7 133.9,123.2 129.0,147.7 132.9,134.0 138.6,88.8 136.9,52.9 136.2,53.4 138.3,82.5 137.1,107.6 149.0,117.4 165.5,121.3 173.8,124.2 161.4,119.7 134.1,107.5 106.2,93.5 103.5,93.3 128.4,104.3 159.9,118.9 180.6,129.6 183.3,131.9 169.3,126.5 141.0,113.4 110.1,99.3 97.7,93.7 121.3,101.5 157.4,114.7 177.7,124.8 174.9,125.4 151.3,112.5 122.1,97.1 95.0,89.7 106.1,93.3 140.9,106.8 168.7,119.3 176.0,124.0 164.5,123.8 144.4,118.4 133.0,110.7 133.0,104.8 134.4,99.1 133.2,95.9 134.5,97.9 139.5,103.4 141.0,107.3 140.6,109.5 139.7,110.8 139.9,107.5 140.0,102.9 141.2,97.5 142.2,97.8 144.3,103.0 144.5,107.0 143.1,110.2 142.3,115.9 142.2,117.9 143.1,108.9 142.7,100.7 143.3,97.0 144.0,97.6 145.1,102.1 143.7,104.9 140.2,109.2 137.6,110.2 136.8,109.5 138.8,104.5 141.2,101.0 142.0,99.5 143.9,100.5 145.9,104.0 144.9,107.4 142.3,113.8 138.4,115.0 136.3,109.6 138.0,102.9 138.9,107.1 137.7,113.9 136.9,119.2 138.2,116.8 140.2,101.6 137.3,87.4 133.0,81.7 135.9,88.8 138.8,102.9 137.8,114.5 135.7,121.5 134.8,123.0 137.7,112.0 137.9,99.7 134.9,92.4 135.3,96.0 136.8,109.5 135.0,123.4 133.3,130.8 136.1,123.2 137.7,110.2 135.2,96.2 133.1,91.8 136.1,101.7 136.7,114.5 136.1,119.4 136.6,116.9 140.3,116.4 144.3,120.1 145.3,122.5 145.0,123.1 140.6,120.0 128.0,115.4 117.2,113.8 114.5,115.4 117.1,116.2 130.3,118.1 142.5,121.7 148.5,125.0 150.3,126.3 149.0,124.0 138.4,118.3 124.3,113.7 115.4,112.7 114.8,112.8 125.2,112.8 139.3,116.7 148.2,121.2 150.1,124.0 149.2,123.8 146.4,121.5 137.8,117.4 124.2,113.1 113.1,111.0 113.2,112.5 118.6,115.4 125.5,119.5 131.7,126.2 129.3,123.1 129.8,116.6 137.2,118.8 142.1,124.4 141.9,126.5 132.7,123.6 124.9,113.0 130.6,108.4 139.4,116.8 142.2,125.2 140.6,128.5 131.2,124.0 127.1,113.4 133.6,112.1 138.6,121.0 138.7,127.2 133.4,128.2 126.0,119.9 126.5,113.8 129.7,115.6 129.9,121.2 128.1,118.5 123.3,117.6 121.3,122.3 123.8,127.9 127.4,130.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg><span>Explore in 3D (about 2 MB)</span></button><div class=\"mvv\" data-mvv=\"scene\" data-mode=\"site\" data-src=\"/media/examples/tum-vi/views0.json\"></div></div>", "result": "<p>The solved positions and orientations, to scale in the IMU frame. Drag sideways to orbit. Tap a sensor to see its values.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>fx, fy, cx, cy px</th><th>Lever mm</th><th>log(R) rad</th><th>td ms</th><th>t_ga ms</th><th>Reprojection px</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>cam0</th><td>382.7, 382.7, 509.8, 514.1</td><td>[+46.8, −69.0, −45.3]</td><td>[−0.0515, −2.1751, +2.2545]</td><td>+0.16</td><td></td><td>0.102</td></tr><tr><th>cam1</th><td>381.3, 381.3, 505.2, 510.1</td><td>[−54.3, −67.5, −48.8]</td><td>[−0.0518, −2.2278, +2.2020]</td><td>+0.16</td><td></td><td>0.096</td></tr><tr><th>IMU (base)</th><td></td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>−1.57 ± 0.30</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Lever arms and rotations are each sensor in the base IMU frame; rotation is log(R) in rad. td is the time offset to the base IMU, t_imu = t_sensor + td. Reprojection is the median per camera (all cameras: median 0.099 px): how well the model fits the corners, not how accurate it is.</p>", "check": "<p>Reference: <a href=\"https://cvg.cit.tum.de/data/datasets/visual-inertial-dataset\">TUM&#x27;s published camera + IMU calibration for the 1024 × 1024 data, Kalibr pinhole-equidistant (the kb4 model), from the TUM VI dataset page</a>.</p><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>MVIS</th><th>TUM (Kalibr)</th><th>Difference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=4>cam0</th></tr><tr><td>Lever mm</td><td>[+46.75, −69.05, −45.30]</td><td>[+45.38, −72.68, −45.07]</td><td>Δp 3.89 mm</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−0.0515, −2.1751, +2.2545]</td><td>[−0.0413, −2.1724, +2.2481]</td><td>Δθ 9.38 mrad</td></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>382.71</td><td>380.81</td><td>Δfx +1.90 px</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>+0.161</td><td>not in TUM&#x27;s calibration file</td><td></td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=4>cam1</th></tr><tr><td>Lever mm</td><td>[−54.32, −67.50, −48.83]</td><td>[−55.52, −71.10, −47.83]</td><td>Δp 3.92 mm</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−0.0518, −2.2278, +2.2020]</td><td>[−0.0417, −2.2243, +2.1962]</td><td>Δθ 9.35 mrad</td></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>381.31</td><td>379.29</td><td>Δfx +2.02 px</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>+0.159</td><td>not in TUM&#x27;s calibration file</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Δp is the distance between the two lever arms. Δθ = ‖log(R<sub>a</sub><sup>T</sup> R<sub>b</sub>)‖, the angle between the two rotations. A reference, not ground truth: it was solved by another tool on the same kind of data.</p><p class=note>The rotation differs by about 9.4 mrad on both cameras. That offset is systematic: MVIS gives the same rotation on all four TUM calibration recordings. It is not explained yet. One possible cause, not verified: this run uses the raw IMU, while TUM&#x27;s Kalibr run used an IMU model it had already calibrated, so the two IMU frames may differ by a small rotation.</p><p class=note>Lens model note: on these lenses the kb4 polynomial folds back inside the image, past about 114° (682 px from the centre) on cam0 and 119° (705 px) on cam1. The model gives no ray beyond that radius.</p>", "config": "<p>The marked lines are the choices that matter for this rig:</p><ul class=list><li><code>input.window_mode</code>: MVIS picks the 80 s window with the most motion.</li><li><code>camera_input.path</code>: Seed intrinsics: kb4 values from MVIS camera-only solves of TUM&#x27;s eight camera recordings.</li><li><code>camera_input.cameras</code>: cam1 is added to the graph at 8 Hz, which keeps the solve small.</li><li><code>solve.estimate_t_ga</code>: Estimates t_ga, the time offset between the gyroscope and the accelerometer.</li><li><code>estimate.camera.intrinsics</code>: Camera intrinsics stay free in the camera + IMU solve.</li><li><code>estimate.imu</code>: The gyro and accelerometer scale and misalignment (dw_da) are estimated too. IMU noise is left at the MVIS defaults.</li></ul><p class=note>This is the config of the run on this page, with every path cut to its file name. Point the paths at your copy.</p><p>The solve took about 4 min on one desktop. It writes <code>cam_imu.json</code>, a calibration YAML and a report beside the config.</p><dl class=ex-kv><dt>MVIS</dt><dd>MVIS main, example solves of 2026-11-10</dd><dt>Run date</dt><dd>2026-11-10</dd><dt>Data</dt><dd><a href=\"https://cvg.cit.tum.de/data/datasets/visual-inertial-dataset\">TUM VI dataset page →</a></dd><dt>Config</dt><dd><code>tum_vi_imu1_cam_imu.yaml</code>, above</dd><dt>Command</dt><dd><code>mvis cam-imu -c tum_vi_imu1_cam_imu.yaml</code></dd></dl>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div><ul class=list><li>Recording dataset-calib-imu1, the first of TUM&#x27;s four camera + IMU calibration recordings, at 1024 × 1024.</li><li>Cameras: two global-shutter fisheye cameras at 20 Hz, fitted with the kb4 (Kannala-Brandt) lens model. IMU: Bosch BMI160 at 200 Hz.</li><li>Board: AprilGrid 6×6, tag 88 mm, spacing 0.3, t36h11.</li><li>Solve window: 48.9 s.</li></ul><p>Download: <a href=\"https://cvg.cit.tum.de/data/datasets/visual-inertial-dataset\">TUM VI dataset page →</a> The recordings are listed there, not copied here.</p></div><div><figure class=board><svg viewBox=\"-52.8 -52.8 765.6 765.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"AprilGrid 6 by 6, to scale\"><rect x=\"-52.8\" y=\"-52.8\" width=\"765.6\" height=\"765.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path fill=\"#111\" d=\"M-26.40 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 202.40h